{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"loveydovey-bouncy-roadrunner","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Live credentials were written into a rebar ticket comment; the tickets branch has been unable to push for ~8 hours\n\nGitHub **push protection** is rejecting every push of the `tickets` branch because one ticket\ncomment contains real secrets. No secret value is reproduced here.\n\n## What was found\n\n    commit  0a09e51c9f   \"ticket: COMMENT 129e-2d88-cce2-492c\"\n    author  RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>\n    when    2026-08-03 19:13:25 -0700\n    path    129e-2d88-cce2-492c/<timestamp>-<uuid>-COMMENT.json\n\nGitHub's scanner names two distinct credential types in that one blob:\n\n  * an **Anthropic API Key**\n  * a **GitHub Personal Access Token**\n\nThe parent ticket is `129e-2d88-cce2-492c` — \"Bedrock cutover silently removed server-side web\nsearch from blocking criterion\" — which belongs to the review-bot / Bedrock workstream, not to\nthe Jira DC epic. The comment appears to have pasted a live environment or provider\nconfiguration verbatim.\n\n## Blast radius\n\n**The secrets did NOT reach GitHub.** `git merge-base --is-ancestor 0a09e51c9f origin/tickets`\nis false — push protection blocked the branch before the commit was ever published. That is the\none piece of good news, and it is luck bought by a platform control rather than by anything\nrebar did.\n\nThey ARE in local git history on the `tickets` branch, on any machine that has fetched or\ncreated it.\n\n**122 ticket commits are stuck behind the blocked one** and cannot reach `origin`. Everything\nwritten to the store from this host since 19:13 is invisible to CI and to every other agent\nsession. Two concrete consequences already observed:\n\n * Gerrit change 1343 fails the `require resolvable rebar ticket` gate — its ticket\n   (`339a-57ac-e5f3-4718`) exists locally but is not on the `tickets` branch CI reads, so the\n   change cannot land.\n * Comments recorded on the Jira DC epic's children tonight are local-only, so the close gates\n   and other sessions cannot see them.\n\nThis also explains why the store's auto-push has been failing silently: rebar writes, commits,\nattempts to push, and the push is rejected — with nothing surfaced to the agent doing the write.\n\n## What must NOT be done\n\n**Do not use the GitHub \"unblock secret\" URL.** It resolves the push by PUBLISHING the\ncredentials to the repository, which is the outcome the control exists to prevent.\n\n## What needs an operator decision\n\n 1. **Rotate both credentials.** They were written into a store whose whole design is to\n    auto-push to a remote; treat them as compromised regardless of the block holding.\n 2. **Remove the comment from the `tickets` branch history.** This is a history rewrite on a\n    shared, auto-pushed branch used by every agent session, so it is not a change any single\n    session should make unilaterally.\n 3. **Consider a store-side guard.** rebar runs `gitleaks` as its code-review secret gate, but\n    nothing scans ticket EVENT payloads on write. A comment is the one place an agent routinely\n    pastes raw environment output, which makes this failure mode likely to recur.\n 4. **Surface a failed auto-push.** The silent failure is arguably the more dangerous defect:\n    the store reported success to every writer for eight hours while diverging from the remote.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] both credentials rotated\n- [ ] the offending comment removed from `tickets` history and the branch pushing again\n- [ ] a rejected auto-push surfaces to the writing agent instead of failing silently\n- [ ] a decision recorded on whether ticket event payloads are scanned on write","id":"94d0-5d19-2d06-4fa7","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live credentials in a rebar ticket comment are blocking every tickets-branch push (122 commits stuck)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785813000370406001,"uuid":"1a3b91ee-a3e2-478f-8682-ff5dcd223299"}